<rml>
<head>
	<title>Achievement unlocked</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="style/base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="style/achievements.rcss"/>
</head>
<!--
	The unlock toast. Its own document because it is shown with or without
	the menu, on the UI clock, for four seconds at a time with the rest
	queued behind it: src/runtime/ui/ui_achievements_model.cpp shows and
	hides it and fills the three strings below from
	src/runtime/guest/achievements.h.

	The whole document is pointer-events: none (see the stylesheet): it is a
	notice, never a control, and a click aimed at the game or at the menu
	must not land on it.
-->
<body class="ach-toast" data-model="achievements">
	<div class="ach-toast-panel">
		<div class="ach-toast-head">
			<span class="ach-toast-tier">{{toast_tier}}</span>
			<span class="ach-toast-label">Achievement unlocked</span>
		</div>
		<div class="ach-toast-name">{{toast_name}}</div>
		<div class="ach-toast-desc">{{toast_description}}</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
